                        "target_lang_word": "triphthong",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "triphthong",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "077f5b13-0e46-38ce-a158-54cfd7027210",
                                        "entry_id": "634b613e-4025-3b71-a5eb-ddb8fe38a0a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A monosyllabic vowel combination usually involving a quick but smooth movement from one vowel to another that passes over a third one."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7de5b96-c7b5-30f0-814d-e29eadf55050",
                                        "entry_id": "634b613e-4025-3b71-a5eb-ddb8fe38a0a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A disyllabic sequence of a vowel, a semivowel, and a vowel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36abb2f9-5f20-467d-a4bf-d602ae1c4074",
                                                "sense_id": "d7de5b96-c7b5-30f0-814d-e29eadf55050",
                                                "text": "Before moving on to a solution, it may be worth emphasizing that nouns of the صلوه type originally contained a triphthong. […] In addition to evidence from the Safaitic inscriptions, the discovery of the Graeco-Arabic inscription A1 (Al-Jallad and al-Manaser 2015), where the verb ’tw ‘he came’ is written αθαοα /’atawa/, confirms this to be the case for Old Arabic as well."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4915c6b-1650-4473-b9c2-0cf20be64414",
                        "source_entry_id": "c81ba41f-ff46-3ec5-8736-0fc4863a47b4",
                        "source_sense_id": "348b7d17-8021-34b4-8c99-047643a55271",
                        "source_sense_description": "akkoord van drie verschillende tonen",
                        "target_lang_word": "Dreiklang",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Dreiklang",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "439ecb0c-cea1-30e7-9f67-9c160185376a",
                                        "entry_id": "2d19e6d9-6d33-3721-99cb-56b8c6d24c49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zusammenklang von drei verschiedenen Tönen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b592e6c4-b306-42e5-bbb5-d5aa202ac298",
                                                "sense_id": "439ecb0c-cea1-30e7-9f67-9c160185376a",
                                                "text": "Der Dreiklang am Schluss eines Satzes ist häufig eine Tonika."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7838ea97-583b-4ba0-b754-07af9a5aa138",
                                                "sense_id": "439ecb0c-cea1-30e7-9f67-9c160185376a",
                                                "text": "„Die Tonfolge eines gebrochenen Dreiklangs, die sich in kurzen Abständen in anschwellendem Maße wiederholte, führte ihn in die Gegenwart zurück.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0d782b37-a318-44a4-8a8e-e96b1c238bba",
                        "source_entry_id": "c81ba41f-ff46-3ec5-8736-0fc4863a47b4",
                        "source_sense_id": "348b7d17-8021-34b4-8c99-047643a55271",
                        "source_sense_description": "akkoord van drie verschillende tonen",
                        "target_lang_word": "triad",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "triad",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cad90b3b-60f5-3d3a-98bf-8aac043d9b9b",
                                        "entry_id": "561b80b6-610a-3296-bc96-74f7cd2a1ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A grouping of three."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "169c0c9d-850c-40a6-8f86-3691c9d8a796",
                                                "sense_id": "cad90b3b-60f5-3d3a-98bf-8aac043d9b9b",
                                                "text": "Later artworks showed many animals and gods, some of which were clearly identified with heavenly body. They often included the symbolic triad of Sun, Moon, and Venus."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69ce098d-5fb9-4e0a-8a3c-3c6a287bc59e",
                                                "sense_id": "cad90b3b-60f5-3d3a-98bf-8aac043d9b9b",
                                                "text": "There are, says the Irish triad, 'three fewnesses that are better than plenty: a fewness of fine words; a fewness of cows on grass; a fewness of good friends around good ale'. As an Ulsterman I would agree."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa049bd8-6491-3bd6-937c-75e4c2a5739d",
                                        "entry_id": "561b80b6-610a-3296-bc96-74f7cd2a1ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A word of three syllables."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "938696ac-3866-4ad9-afed-d05e830a1dc4",
                                                "sense_id": "fa049bd8-6491-3bd6-937c-75e4c2a5739d",
                                                "text": "In his general deportment he was pompous and important, affecting a species of florid elocution, which often became ridiculous from his misarranging the triads and quaternions with which he loaded his sentences."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64fecdbd-d063-3eb2-89c6-33ff187b2b4b",
                                        "entry_id": "561b80b6-610a-3296-bc96-74f7cd2a1ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A branch of a Chinese underground criminal society, mostly based in Hong Kong."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c56ca2e5-a058-4873-8670-b9ab5b968fd8",
                                                "sense_id": "64fecdbd-d063-3eb2-89c6-33ff187b2b4b",
                                                "text": "The point — and the symbolism — was that so long as the informer kept his mouth shut he was alive. Harry had seen the result of zjuk carried out by the Tapei Triad on a poor jerk they found in a back street of Tan-shui. They had used broad nail heads that didn’t make such big holes on their way in. When the paramedics came and pulled the brick off the dead man, the face came with it.",
                                                "translation": "Phantom",
                                                "english": "Phantom"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c924b32-7d86-3eed-ab2d-0256562ac4be",
                                        "entry_id": "561b80b6-610a-3296-bc96-74f7cd2a1ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On a CRT display, a group of three neighbouring phosphor dots, coloured green, red, and blue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a9aab02-1833-3568-85b1-71fd3475c996",
                                        "entry_id": "561b80b6-610a-3296-bc96-74f7cd2a1ece",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A chord consisting of a root tone, the tone two degrees higher, and the tone four degrees higher in a given scale OR any chord with three notes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed644b4c-a622-4bdd-887e-f5f29efaec14",
                        "source_entry_id": "c81ba41f-ff46-3ec5-8736-0fc4863a47b4",
                        "source_sense_id": "348b7d17-8021-34b4-8c99-047643a55271",
